<h2 class="mt-6">Features</h2>
<div class="l-ui-grid mt-4">
  <div class="l-ui-surface flex items-center gap-4">
    <%= image_tag "layered_ui/icon_code_bracket.svg", class: "l-ui-icon l-ui-icon--xl", alt: "", aria: { hidden: true } %>
    <div>
      <h3>Skip the boilerplate</h3>
      <p>Declare your columns, fields, and search - get index, show, forms, search, sort, and pagination for free. No scaffold to maintain, no half-finished admin gem to fight.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="l-ui-surface flex items-center gap-4">
    <%= image_tag "icon_paint.svg", class: "l-ui-icon l-ui-icon--xl", alt: "", aria: { hidden: true } %>
    <div>
      <h3>Looks right out of the box</h3>
      <p>Tables, forms, and pagination come pre-styled via <a href="https://github.com/layered-ai-public/layered-ui-rails">layered-ui-rails</a> with WCAG 2.2 AA compliance and dark mode included.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="l-ui-surface flex items-center gap-4">
    <%= image_tag "icon_wrench.svg", class: "l-ui-icon l-ui-icon--xl", alt: "", aria: { hidden: true } %>
    <div>
      <h3>Override only what you need</h3>
      <p>Swap a single view partial, subclass the controller for a custom scope or redirect, or generate plain ERB to take full control - without rewriting the rest.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="l-ui-surface flex items-center gap-4">
    <%= image_tag "icon_eject.svg", class: "l-ui-icon l-ui-icon--xl", alt: "", aria: { hidden: true } %>
    <div>
      <h3>Eject cleanly if you outgrow it</h3>
      <p>Generate a standard Rails controller and views, drop the gem, and you're left with idiomatic Rails. No lock-in, no hidden coupling.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
